## ✅ 4. Laravel Validation Rules

You can use these in your `FormRequest` or controller:

```php
$rules = [
    'user_id' => 'required|exists:users,id',
    'service_id' => 'required|exists:services,id',
    'appointment_date' => [
        'required',
        'date',
        function ($attribute, $value, $fail) use ($service) {
            $today = now()->toDateString();
            $maxDate = now()->addDays($service->max_booking_days_ahead)->toDateString();
            if ($value < $today || $value > $maxDate) {
                $fail("Booking must be between today and {$service->max_booking_days_ahead} days ahead.");
            }
        },
        function ($attribute, $value, $fail) use ($service) {
            if ($service->closedDates()->where('closed_date', $value)->exists()) {
                $fail("This date is closed for the selected service.");
            }
        }
    ],
    'start_time' => 'required|date_format:H:i',
    'end_time' => 'required|date_format:H:i|after:start_time',
    'number_of_clients' => [
        'required',
        'integer',
        function ($attribute, $value, $fail) use ($service) {
            if ($value > $service->max_clients_per_slot) {
                $fail("Maximum {$service->max_clients_per_slot} clients allowed per slot.");
            }
        }
    ]
];
```

