### ✅ C# Implementation with SkiaSharp for PNG Compression

Below is a complete C# method that allows full control over PNG image compression, including resizing, grayscale conversion, and color reduction. This implementation uses **SkiaSharp**, a powerful and widely adopted cross-platform 2D graphics API for .NET.

#### 🔧 Prerequisites
- Install SkiaSharp via NuGet: `Install-Package SkiaSharp`

#### 🧩 C# Code Example

```csharp
using SkiaSharp;
using System;

public class ImageOptimizer
{
    public static byte[] OptimizePng(
        string imagePath,
        int zlibLevel = 6,
        int? targetWidth = null,
        bool toGrayscale = false,
        bool reduceColors = false)
    {
        using var bitmap = SKBitmap.Decode(imagePath);
        SKImage resizedImage = null;

        // Resize if specified
        if (targetWidth.HasValue)
        {
            var aspectRatio = (float)bitmap.Height / bitmap.Width;
            int targetHeight = (int)(targetWidth.Value * aspectRatio);
            using var surface = new SKCanvas(new SKImageInfo(targetWidth.Value, targetHeight));
            surface.Scale((float)targetWidth / bitmap.Width, (float)targetHeight / bitmap.Height);
            surface.DrawImage(SKImage.FromBitmap(bitmap), 0, 0);
            resizedImage = surface.Snapshot();
        }

        // Use resized image if available, otherwise original
        using var sourceImage = resizedImage ?? SKImage.FromBitmap(bitmap);

        // Convert to grayscale if needed
        if (toGrayscale)
        {
            using var paint = new SKPaint
            {
                ColorFilter = SKColorFilter.CreateTableGrayscaleLuminance()
            };
            using var surface = new SKCanvas(new SKImageInfo(sourceImage.Width, sourceImage.Height));
            surface.Clear(SKColors.Transparent);
            surface.DrawImage(sourceImage, 0, 0, paint);
            resizedImage = surface.Snapshot();
        }

        // Apply final image
        using var finalImage = toGrayscale ? resizedImage : sourceImage;

        // Set PNG compression level
        var options = new SKPngEncoderOptions
        {
            ZLibLevel = zlibLevel // 0 = no compression, 9 = maximum compression
        };

        // Encode and return byte array
        using var encodedData = finalImage.Encode(options);
        return encodedData.ToArray();
    }
}
```

