% 2. Ensure proper randomness - use SecureRandom instead of standard RNG
% 3. Don't implement crypto operations from scratch in production
% 4. Validate inputs to prevent side-channel attacks
% 5. Handle key storage securely - don't hardcode keys in source code
% 6. Use established libraries for real-world applications (e.g., OpenSSL)
% 7. Avoid predictable prime generation patterns
% 8. Always verify primality with multiple Miller-Rabin tests
% 9. Ensure proper error handling for modular inverse operations
